Description: Implements anytime-valid one-sample t-tests for a Gaussian
    mean with unknown variance. Fixed priors on the standardized effect
    size are combined with Ville or extended Ville calibration to obtain
    running p-values and first rejection times. Supports Gaussian and
    Cauchy priors, one-sided and two-sided alternatives, and separately
    calibrated Lebesgue benchmarks. Provides summaries and plots of
    sequential test results.
